The `Get Blob` operation reads or downloads a blob from the system, including its metadata and properties. You can also call `Get Blob` to read a snapshot.

[Section titled: Request](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/get-blob?tabs=microsoft-entra-id#request)

## Request

You can construct the `Get Blob` request as follows. We recommend that you use HTTPS. Replace _myaccount_ with the name of your storage account:

Expand table

| GET method request URI | HTTP version |
| --- | --- |
| `https://myaccount.blob.core.windows.net/mycontainer/myblob`<br>`https://myaccount.blob.core.windows.net/mycontainer/myblob?snapshot=<DateTime>`<br>`https://myaccount.blob.core.windows.net/mycontainer/myblob?versionid=<DateTime>` | HTTP/1.0<br> HTTP/1.1 |

[Section titled: Emulated storage service URI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/get-blob?tabs=microsoft-entra-id#emulated-storage-service-uri)

### Emulated storage service URI

When you're making a request against the emulated storage service, specify the emulator hostname and Azure Blob Storage port as `127.0.0.1:10000`, followed by the emulated storage account name:

Expand table

| GET method request URI | HTTP version |
| --- | --- |
| `http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1/mycontainer/myblob` | HTTP/1.0<br> HTTP/1.1 |

For more information, see [Use the Azure Storage Emulator for development and testing](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/storage-use-emulator).

[Section titled: URI parameters](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/get-blob?tabs=microsoft-entra-id#uri-parameters)

### URI parameters

The following additional parameters may be specified on the request URI:

Expand table

